00:00:31.902 --> 00:00:33.929
Don't hash and hope for no collisions.

10
00:00:34.209 --> 00:00:41.526
Allocate a unique id (a DB sequence, or per-node ranges from a counter service), then base62-encode it.

11
00:00:41.806 --> 00:00:46.777
Seven characters cover 62⁷ about 3.5 trillion URLs.

12
00:00:47.057 --> 00:00:53.179
Custom aliases live in the same keyspace and are claimed atomically (putIfAbsent here; INSERT...

13
